note bottom of UC_Constrain
  Extension point: "a selection exists".
  When it does, Paint, Erase, Fill and Clear selection contents only affect cells inside the selection.
  Without a selection the whole page is editable. Invert selection flips what is inside.
end note

note bottom of UC_Close
  "Save project" extends "Close project" at the extension point "project has unsaved changes":
  the user is asked Save / Discard / Cancel before the project is closed.
end note

note bottom of UC_Bg
  Each frame owns its own background colour: the opaque page colour UNDER the whole layer stack.
  New frames copy the background of the selected frame; duplicated frames copy their source.
  Cells whose mixed background is transparent show this colour; exports use it too.
end note

note bottom of UC_Rect
  The three selection use cases (square, polygon, ellipse) create the selection that activates the
  "Constrain edits to selection" extension. Replace / Add / Subtract buttons in the top bar, or Shift = add, Alt = subtract while selecting.
end note

note bottom of UC_Paint
  There is no typing on the canvas. The character comes from the chosen brush (a stamp of one or more characters),
  the colours from the top bar. The planes switch decides what is written: Foreground = character + character colour,
  Background = cell fill colour (both colours may have transparency). Custom brushes are created in the Brush editor.
end note

note bottom of UC_Move
  Needs a selection. "Contents" lifts the selected cells of the ACTIVE layer and drops them somewhere else (undoable, the selection moves along).
  "Outline only" moves just the selection marks. Arrow keys nudge by one cell.
end note

note bottom of UC_Paste
  Paste always creates a NEW layer above the active one that holds only the copied selection, at its original position,
  selected and ready to be dragged with Move. Copy takes the active layer; "Copy merged" takes what is visible.
end note

note bottom of UC_Import
  .txt: every line is a row, every character a cell (spaces stay empty), drawn in the chosen character colour.
  .ascii: the flattened image with its own colours. The result is added as a new layer above the active one.
  "Suggest growing the project" extends Import at the extension point "file is wider or taller than the project": the user may accept
  (project grows, then import) or refuse (the file is simply added as a layer and cut off at the page border).
end note

note bottom of UC_PickCanvas
  Picks the colour of the clicked cell for the plane(s) switched on: Foreground -> character colour, Background -> background fill colour.
  Source = merged result (default) or the active layer only.
end note

note bottom of UC_LNew
  Shared step of Paste and Import: build a full-page layer from a snippet, insert it above the active layer, make it active,
  select its cells. One undo step.
end note
